++# Sort the report by cents
++
++Date: 2026-11-20. Branch: `feature/report-sort`.
++
++## Context and goal
++
++`tally report` lists every account with its balance, in account order. A script that wants the largest balances has to
++sort the rows itself. `report` gets a `--sort <key>` option, so that `tally report --json --sort cents` prints the rows
++with the largest balance first.
++
++## Behaviour
++
++- `tally report [--json] [--sort account|cents]`.
++- `--sort account` is the default and today's order: ascending by account.
++- `--sort cents` orders the rows by balance, largest first; rows with the same balance stay in account order.
++- A key other than `account` or `cents` fails with `sort must be account or cents` on stderr and exit code 1. `--sort`
++  with no key after it prints the usage text and exits 1.
++- The key applies to the plain output and to `--json`; the shape of a row does not change.
++
++## Design
++
++- `report(db, { sort = 'account' } = {})` in `src/ledger.js` takes the key and throws `Error('sort must be account or
++  cents')` for any other. The query keeps `ORDER BY account`; the `cents` order is a stable sort over its rows, so ties
++  keep account order. The key never reaches the SQL text.
++- `showReport` in `bin/tally` reads the key with `flagValue(args, '--sort')` and passes it to `report`; the `USAGE` text
++  and the README's command list name the option.
++
++## Decisions and the pages they change
++
++No decision of this branch changes a protected page: the project protects none.
++
++## Testing
++
++Unit tests only: `test/unit/ledger.test.js` for `report`, `test/unit/cli.test.js` for the CLI. No end-to-end scenario.
